#: data/io.github.cheviiot.bastle.metainfo.xml.in:28
msgid ""
"Bastle is a GNOME-native manager for isolated web applications. WebKitGTK is "
"the default engine, and Chromium is available as a Flatpak add-on for "
"explicitly selected sites. Each website gets separate local data, cookies, "
"cache, settings, and its own desktop launcher."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.cheviiot.bastle.metainfo.xml.in:34
msgid ""
"Bastle is an independent successor to Spider. The original work by Zaedus, "
"Cameron Radmore's contribution, and their Git history remain credited. "
"Bastle is developed independently and does not claim their endorsement or "
"participation."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.cheviiot.bastle.metainfo.xml.in:41
msgid "Create, edit, repair, and remove portal-installed launchers"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.cheviiot.bastle.metainfo.xml.in:42
msgid "Fetch and safely normalize website icons with an offline fallback"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.cheviiot.bastle.metainfo.xml.in:43
msgid ""
"Keep each application's configuration, policy, profile, and cache separate"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.cheviiot.bastle.metainfo.xml.in:58
msgid "Move the Chromium payload from the main app into a Flatpak add-on"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.cheviiot.bastle.metainfo.xml.in:59
msgid "Publish the app and add-on together from the signed Bastle repository"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.cheviiot.bastle.metainfo.xml.in:60
msgid "Keep WebKitGTK usable when the Chromium add-on is not installed"
msgstr ""

